<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amursana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1723–1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amursana was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> prince of the Khoit tribe who took part in the succession struggles of the Dzungar Khanate in the 1750s. After falling out with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawachi">Dawachi</a>, the khan he had helped to power, he submitted to the Qing in 1754 and guided their armies into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a>. When the Qing denied him rule over the Oirats he revolted in 1755, was defeated and died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> in Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amursana.jpg" alt="Amursana" width="292" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amursana.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
